interface_contract:
CONSUMED (owned by be-28-02, scripts/chain/evidence.mjs — do not redefine):
Baseline = { anchor_sha: string, reason: string, captured_at: string, dirty: { [path]: { xy: string, sha256: string|null } } }
Touched = { paths: string[], sources: { committed: string[], dirty: string[], reverted: string[] } }
RunResult = { cmd, argv, code: number|null, classified: 'exit'|'timeout'|'missing_binary'|'signal'|'signal_unknown'|'refused', signal: string|null, elapsed_ms: number, ok: boolean, tail: string, log_path: string, note: string }
Exports: captureBaseline, readBaseline, writeBaselineExclusive, touchedPaths, runValidationCommand, GATE_RUN_TIMEOUT_MS, EvidenceError, EVIDENCE_ERROR_CODES.

CONSUMED (owned by be-28-01, scripts/cmux/return-lint.mjs):
extractVerdictBlock(body: string) -> { ok: true, verdict: 'pass'|'changes-needed'|'inconclusive', findings: object[] } | { ok: false, keyword: string, message: string }

PRODUCED (backend owns; this is the stdout contract every future chain consumer reads):
Check = { item: string, ok: boolean, hard_fail: boolean, note: string }
  NOTE a deliberate extension of issue #28's three-field {item, ok, note} sketch: hard_fail is a REQUIRED fourth field on every check, always a boolean and never absent, so the top-level hard_fail is derivable and every consumer can compare with === true and fail closed on a malformed check.
Violation = { item: string, hard_fail: boolean, note: string }
GateReport = {
  task: string,
  slice: string,
  checks: Check[],
  hard_fail: boolean,        // === checks.some(c => c.hard_fail === true)
  violations: Violation[]    // === checks.filter(c => c.ok === false).map(c => ({item, hard_fail, note}))
}
CHECK_NAMES (frozen) = ['artifacts_exist','files_non_empty','json_parses','diff_matches_claims','scope_compliance','spec_lint','tests_pass','verdict_consistent']
PROTECTED_PREFIXES (frozen) = ['.claude/dev-team/memory/', '.claude/dev-team/config.md']
Exit codes: 0 = no violations · 1 = violations present (read hard_fail from the JSON) · 2 = usage/operational error.
Exported pure check functions (all take collected inputs, return Check or Check[]): checkArtifacts, checkFilesNonEmpty, checkJsonParses, checkDiffMatchesClaims, checkScopeCompliance, checkSpecLint, checkTestsPass, checkVerdictConsistent, buildReport, runChecks(ctx, io), main(argv) -> number.
